@using FellowshipAnalyzer.Core.Common.Spells.Tariq
@using Spells = FellowshipAnalyzer.Core.Common.Spells.Tariq.Spells

<GuideContainer>
    <Section Title="Overview">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                Tariq is a melee DPS built around a build-and-spend resource system. He generates
                <strong>Fury</strong> with his basic and core abilities, then spends it on high-damage
                power abilities. Everything revolves around pooling Fury outside of
                <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> and dumping it during the empowered window.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Core Mechanic — Fury">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                Fury caps at 100. It is generated by Basic abilities
                (<SpellLink Spell="Spells.WildSwing" />, <SpellLink Spell="Spells.FaceBreaker" />) and
                Core abilities (<SpellLink Spell="Spells.HeavyStrike" />,
                <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ChainLightning" />), and spent by Power abilities
                (<SpellLink Spell="Spells.HammerStorm" />, <SpellLink Spell="Spells.SkullCrusher" />,
                <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" />).
            </p>
            <p>
                Pool Fury while <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> is on cooldown, then maximize
                spending during the <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> window for the biggest
                damage payoff.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
        <TipBox Variant="TipBoxVariant.Note" Title="Don't overcap">
            Fury sitting at 100 is wasted generation. If you are near cap outside the
            <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> window, spend it rather than losing it.
        </TipBox>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Rotation">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                Tariq follows a priority system rather than a fixed rotation. Work down the list and
                cast the highest available entry. The single-target and AoE lists share the same
                cooldowns and generators but differ on which Fury spender to favour.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
        <SubSection Title="Single-Target Priority">
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <strong>Weapon ability</strong> (Sahril's Reckoning, Fateful Basher, or
                    Void-Touched Hammer) lined up with <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> /
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.RagingTempest" />.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.RagingTempest" /> →
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> →
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.FocusedWrath" />.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Free <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> procs from
                    <strong>Executioner's Unsanitary Bands</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" /> for <strong>Slayer's Mosh</strong> with
                    <strong>Drape Of The Slayer King</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> at 10+ Fury; prioritize it below 30%
                    target health as an execute.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.SkullCrusher" /> on 1–2 targets during the
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> window or when Fury is capped.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HeavyStrike" /> to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" /> with the <strong>High Road</strong> talent
                    to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ChainLightning" /> to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.WildSwing" /> as filler.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </SubSection>
        <SubSection Title="AoE Priority (3+ targets)">
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <strong>Weapon ability</strong> (Sahril's Reckoning, Fateful Basher, or
                    Void-Touched Hammer) lined up with <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> /
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.RagingTempest" />.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.RagingTempest" /> →
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> →
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.FocusedWrath" />.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Free <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> procs from
                    <strong>Executioner's Unsanitary Bands</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" /> for <strong>Slayer's Mosh</strong> with
                    <strong>Drape Of The Slayer King</strong>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> at 10+ Fury; prioritize it below 30%
                    target health as an execute.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HammerStorm" /> on 3+ targets during the
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ThunderCall" /> window or when Fury is capped.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HeavyStrike" /> to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" /> with the <strong>High Road</strong> talent
                    to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.FaceBreaker" /> as an AoE generator on the non-lightning
                    build.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.ChainLightning" /> to generate Fury.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <SpellLink Spell="Spells.WildSwing" /> as filler.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </SubSection>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Mechanics">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> and <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" />
                are off-GCD and can be used immediately, but they interrupt
                <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HammerStorm" />'s channel — hold them until the channel finishes.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
        <TipBox Variant="TipBoxVariant.Warning" Title="Execute phase">
            Below 30% target health, prioritize <SpellLink Spell="Spells.CullingStrike" /> whenever you
            have 10+ Fury.
        </TipBox>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Talents & Builds">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                <strong>Schism</strong>: use <SpellLink Spell="Spells.SkullCrusher" /> in all situations
                and only cast <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HammerStorm" /> on a Schism proc.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Kill 'em All</strong>: grants <SpellLink Spell="Spells.HeavyStrike" /> resets and
                empowerment procs lasting 8 seconds — consume them quickly before they expire.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Tips">
        <ul>
            <li>Keybind <strong>Mark Unit</strong> / <strong>Mark Location</strong> for target designation.</li>
            <li>Use quick-cast targeting for instant <SpellLink Spell="Spells.LeapSmash" /> placement.</li>
            <li>Configure buff/debuff displays so proc windows stay visible.</li>
        </ul>
    </Section>

    <TipBox Variant="TipBoxVariant.Info" Title="Source">
        Adapted from the community
        <a href="https://www.method.gg/fellowship/heroes/tariq/playstyle-and-rotation"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">method.gg Tariq guide</a>.
    </TipBox>
</GuideContainer>
